SimuCell3D
==========

SimuCell3D was created by Steve Runser in the group of Dagmar Iber (Iber Lab) at the
Department of Biosystems Science and Engineering (D-BSSE) of ETH Zurich and the Swiss
Institute of Bioinformatics (SIB), Basel, and is described in

    Runser, S., Vetter, R. & Iber, D. SimuCell3D: three-dimensional simulation of tissue
    mechanics with cell polarization. Nat. Comput. Sci. 4, 299-309 (2024).
    https://doi.org/10.1038/s43588-024-00620-9

Release 1.0 was distributed by its authors under the 3-Clause BSD License. The file LICENSE
reproduces that licence text verbatim, as it appears in the file `License` of release 1.0
(tag v1.0); the original file names no copyright holder.

